Definitions

"Owner", "we" and "us" mean Guillaume Huard Hughes, the copyright
holder.

"You" means any person or organization that gets, uses or reads the
Software.

"Software" means Gitnetix: the source code, builds, installers, icons,
logos, website and documentation in this repository, and any part of
them.

"Derivative" means anything copied from the Software or built from its
code, in whole or in substantial part. An exact copy is a Derivative.
So is a modified, renamed, rebranded or translated version, and a port
of the code to another language or framework.

"Contribution" means any code, text, design, translation or other
material you send to the official Gitnetix project, for example in a
pull request, an issue or a comment.


1. What you may do

a. Download, install and use the official builds of Gitnetix for free,
   on any number of devices, for personal and work projects, including
   commercial ones.
b. Read and study the source code.
c. Build and run the Software from source on your own devices, to try
   it, learn from it or test a change.
d. Fork the official repository on the platform that hosts it, and
   change your fork, to prepare a Contribution. You may not publish
   builds of the fork or present it as a separate product.
e. Share links to the official repository and the official download
   page.
f. Quote short parts of the code in a bug report, a review, a
   discussion or an article about Gitnetix.


2. What you may not do

Unless the owner gives you written permission, you may not:

a. Distribute, publish, host or share the Software or a Derivative, as
   source code or as a build, beyond what section 1 allows. This
   includes free and non-commercial releases.
b. Sell, rent, lease or sublicense the Software or a Derivative, charge
   for access to it, or include it in a product or service you sell or
   offer to others.
c. Release an app, product or service that copies the Software or is
   built from its code, in whole or in substantial part.
d. Use the Gitnetix name, logo or icons for another product, or in a
   way that suggests the owner made, approved or supports your work.
e. Remove or change this license or any copyright notice in the
   Software.


3. Your projects stay yours

This license covers Gitnetix itself. It gives the owner no rights in
the repositories, code or other work you manage with Gitnetix.


